Package: biomimic
Title: A Pipeline from Omics Features to Structural Equation Models
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alexandre Henrique Carvalho", "Marques", email = "alexandre.marques.088@ufrn.edu.br",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Dennyson Leandro M.", "Fonseca", role = "aut"),
    person("Tiberio Azevedo", "Pereira", role = "ctb"),
    person("Rita Maria Cunha", "de Almeida", role = "ctb"),
    person("Otavio", "Cabral-Marques", role = "aut"),
    person("Rodrigo Juliani Siqueira", "Dalmolin", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Takes high-dimensional omics data to structural equation
    models fitted with 'lavaan'. Features are ranked by group association
    ('limma', 'cate', or a variational Bayes factor model with automatic
    relevance determination, VB-ARD), grouped into modules ('WGCNA', curated
    gene sets or VB-ARD factors) and checked against each sample's global
    level before modelling. The chosen panels are then fitted as
    multi-factor MIMIC models, tested for measurement invariance, used to
    split each feature's group effect into parts through each factor and an
    own part, entered as latent mediators, separated from a general factor
    in bifactor models, or followed over repeated measures with
    within-between splits and random-intercept cross-lagged panel models
    (Hamaker, Kuiper and Grasman 2015 <doi:10.1037/a0038889>). Models report
    likelihood-ratio tests, fit indices and residual diagnostics. VB-ARD
    estimates factors and each feature's direct effect jointly; it is one
    front end among several, not a replacement for the others. Written for
    antibodyome, proteomics and transcriptomics studies.
